  "body": "#2257: while an operation generates its toolpath, the viewport shows no progress. The cause is that generation ran in the frame, on the UI thread. Thus no frame painted until the job ended.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Generation on a worker** (native window only). `GenerateOperation` already had a seam between the world reads and the pure work (M5.3 B). That seam is now public as `StagedGeneration`:\n  - `StagedGeneration::new` reads the world on the UI thread.\n  - `StagedGeneration::finish` runs the generator, the verification and the stamp on a worker thread.\n  - The result lands through the same undoable `GenerateOperation` as before. The generators, the verify check and the post gate do not change.\n- **The overlay** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/gen_overlay.rs`) lies at the top centre of the viewport while a job runs. The navigation strip at the bottom and the view cube stay clear. It shows:\n  - the label of the operation;\n  - \"(2 of 5)\" when more generations wait in the queue;\n  - the elapsed time and an activity bar (the generators report no fraction);\n  - a `Cancel generation` button.\n- **Stale results are discarded.** The user can edit, undo or delete while the worker runs. A result lands only while its operation and its cached path are the same as at staging (`GenerateOperation::still_current`). If not, the status line says: `generation of X discarded: the operation changed while it generated - generate it again`.\n- **Cancel** drops the result and the queue. The old toolpath stays. A worker that runs finishes in the background, and its result is ignored.\n- **New and Open** drop a running generation. A result for the old document never lands in the new one.\n- **The viewport takes no press inside the overlay.** A click on Cancel is not also a viewport pick.\n- **Only the window turns it on** (`State::gen_jobs.background`). Tests, headless runs, scripts and MCP keep the synchronous path. `State::settle` waits for the worker. The browser has no threads: a failed spawn runs the job in place, as the import worker does.\n- **Repaint:** the shell asks for a repaint every 50 ms only while a job runs or waits (`view_pass::state_redraw_delay`). A frame with no job does no more work than before (#2238).\n- **No world search in a frame.** The job finds its operation entity one time, when it starts. Each frame reads the label from that entity (`model::live_operation_label`, which checks that the entity is alive). A rename shows at once. A deleted operation shows its name.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2257-generate-progress-overlay.md`.\n\n## What it looks like\n\nRendered headless from the seeded shell at 1280x800 (a throwaway test, not in the branch). The images are below.\n\n- Before: while `Contour1` generates, the viewport shows nothing.\n- After: the overlay at the top centre, with the operation name, the elapsed time, the activity bar and `Cancel generation`.\n\n**Before** (the viewport while `Contour1` generates):\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"800\" alt=\"before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8944b68f-cbf0-4c89-8c6e-caf2c29d55b5\" />\n\n**After** (the overlay at the top centre):\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"800\" alt=\"after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19c4a38b-2042-4cff-a14c-87059e622d40\" />\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pinning tests:\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/generate_progress.rs` (structural; the result comes through a channel that the test holds, so no frame races a real generator):\n  - `the_overlay_names_the_running_operation_and_goes_when_it_lands`: the overlay text `Generating Contour1 - ...` is over the viewport, and the Cancel button is there while the job runs. The two go when the job lands.\n  - `a_refusal_ends_the_overlay_and_keeps_its_message`\n  - `cancel_ends_the_overlay_and_drops_the_result`: a click on Cancel ends the overlay. The status says that the generation is cancelled. No history entry is written.\n  - `a_result_for_an_operation_edited_meanwhile_is_discarded`: the edit stays, and the old result writes nothing.\n  - `background_generation_lands_the_same_toolpath`: a real worker run through `settle`.\n  - `the_overlay_text_counts_a_batch`\n  - `one_search_for_each_job_and_a_rename_shows_without_another`: 10 frames and 100 progress reads do one name search. A rename shows in the overlay with no new search.\n  - `a_deleted_operation_shows_its_name_and_no_dead_entity_is_read`: the overlay shows `Contour1` after a delete. Without the `is_alive` check, the test process stops (0xc0000409).\n- `crates/app/tests/generate_staged.rs`:\n  - `staged_then_finished_lands_what_the_one_shot_command_lands`: the same path either way.\n  - `a_result_is_stale_after_an_edit_a_generation_or_a_delete`\n\nGates on 08022981:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (222 steps): green, with two exceptions. Neither comes from this change:\n  - `app suites: wire_tool` does not compile on main. That is #2244 (`CuttingRow` gained `stepdown` and `stepover`).\n  - `ui suites: lib`: three tests in `setup_picks_disarm` failed one time. They pass alone. The same suite on a clean `upstream/main` worktree fails 1 of 3 runs at `--test-threads=16` (`setup_picks_disarm`, `setup_mount_pages`). Thus the failures are timing failures on main.\n- `generate_progress` (6) and `generate_staged` (2): green after the last layout change.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --bins --test generate_staged -- -D warnings`: clean. `--all-targets` stops at `wire_tool` (#2244).\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\nReview fix on 43b789ed (label read from the entity):\n\n- `generate_progress` (8): green.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` at `--test-threads=16`: 1025 passed, 0 failed.\n- `generate_staged` (2): green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `model.rs` gets 7 lines (`live_operation_label`). The file was 482 lines before this change. The helper is next to `operation_label`, because the UI crate does no raw world call.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No hand test in the real window on a long job. The structural tests drive the same `viewport_panel` code through the harness.\n- `RegenerateAll` (the batch fix of the stale operations) stays synchronous. Its rounds write the world between rounds, so it does not split at one seam. It shows no overlay. The overlay's \"n of m\" counts single generations that wait in the queue.\n- The browser build was not run. Its generation stays synchronous through the spawn fallback.\n\nChangelog: While a toolpath generates, a progress overlay over the viewport names the operation, counts the queued ones and offers Cancel; the window stays responsive (#2257)\n\nEffort: medium (the label of the issue). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #2257\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
